ne priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably.\n- Norvane plans 2027 capex up 12%. Debt probably covers it.\n\n**Equity: weak.**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- Norvane's own equity access hasn't been tested.\n\n**Pellham is the stress case.**\n- It plans 2027 capex up 18% and is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- It is now cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\".\n- Debt alone appears unable to cover the gap left by the failed equity raise. The sources don't say why. Leverage or rating limits are possible, but I haven't confirmed either.\n\n**Limits of the evidence.** It rests on three documents: one failed equity deal, two downsized deals and one successful bond. They give no total funding needs, balance-sheet headroom, credit ratings or equity valuations, so I can't size the shortfall.\n\n**Implication.** Capex that depends on equity is likely to slip, as Pellham's already has. Stronger issuers can probably fund their plans with debt.\n\nMy two child nodes reached the same conclusion: n5 on debt (n5.r1) and n6 on equity (n6.r1).","ttft_ms":1886,"type":"result","duration_ms":33813,"uuid":"11bdd8d6-d32d-473e-aa03-c8485375fd94","ttft_stream_ms":1244,"time_to_request_ms":452,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":57,"system_prompt":18,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":13,"input_attachments":92,"input_hooks":16,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":67,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":19,"init_frame_send":22,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":22,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":47,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":12,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":10,"client_creation":14,"request_build":24},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":222,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":89,"t